-- =========================================================================
-- Prover — untrusted proposers + the kernel trust-boundary, declared as
-- `@native` foreign decls + the 5 surviving Curry-Howard ADT entities
-- (Proposition/ProofTerm RETIRED — decide-substrate Phase 2 K4, see below).
--
-- Phase 4 / Phase 8 / Phase 12 of the implementation roadmap. Each proposer
-- takes a CLAIM — the one lattice `Judgment` (JEmpty/JInhabited,
-- engine/judgment.fenel) or a compat Prop* marker — and returns
-- `Result UnprovedReason <proof marker>` (the standard Prover.propose
-- signature) — they are UNTRUSTED: the kernel (engine/src/kernel.ts, exposed
-- as `kernel:verify`) re-checks every term they produce before promotion to a
-- theorem.
--
-- module-substrate Phase 3i (close-out, 2026-05-31) — the both-maps capstone.
-- The ~1178-LOC hand-assembled engine/src/modules/prover.ts (7 defineFunction
-- specs + the 6 inline `$variant` entity literals + the inline native impls) is
-- RETIRED. This file carries the declarative half: 6 @native decls + the 6 ADTs.
-- The impls live in ffi/prover-ffi.ts; the 8 Prover dispatch instances stay in
-- instances.fenel (the seam projects them).
--
-- TWO intricate reconciliations (preserved byte-for-byte):
--   1. codeName ≠ fnId-suffix on ALL FOUR *Propose fns: id `prover:<name>`,
--      codeName + native-map key `<name>Propose` (the native key rides the
--      codeName via rekeyNativesById, NOT the fnId). Carried by @codeName.
--   2. `kernel:verify` cross-prefix: authored here as `prover:kernelVerify`
--      (the `prover:`-prefixing header), re-id'd to `kernel:verify` in the seam;
--      its native is re-added at the explicit `kernel:kernelVerify` key.
--
-- PARTIAL 3/7 both-maps: reductionProver / compilableSemanticCheck /
-- partialEvaluatorSoundnessCheck register in BOTH the plain + ctx native maps
-- (seam-routed — no @nativeCtx marker, axis #4); the other 4 are plain-only.
--
-- No @category anywhere: the 6 prover: fns derive "prover" + kernel:verify
-- derives "kernel" at read time (displayCategory → the id's module-prefix),
-- byte-equal to the retired `category: "prover"` / `"kernel"` (Phase 3j: store
-- only NON-derivable display). Counterexample payloads use the owned universal
-- `Anything`; scalar fields retain `String` / `Number` / `Boolean` —
-- exact type-shape byte-equality is not required for parity, but the entity
-- ROSTER + case-name rosters + the field NAMES (which drive `_constructors`)
-- match the retired inline literals.
-- =========================================================================

module prover where

using system (Anything)

-- ----- Curry-Howard ADT entities ----------------------------------------

-- THE CLOSED SUMS ARE RETIRED (decide-substrate Phase 2 K4). The `Proposition`
-- (6-case) and `ProofTerm` (3-rule) entity decls that lived here are GONE —
-- the closed ADTs died into the one-lattice-judgment vocabulary:
--
--   • The CLAIM currency is the registered `Judgment` (JEmpty / JInhabited,
--     `fenel/modules/engine/judgment.fenel`) — built via the judgment
--     constructors + the composed-set builders (`jopSubset` / `jopDisjoint`)
--     + the positional builder faces (`propSubset` / `propDisjoint` /
--     `propEmpty` / `propInhabited`, same file): the Prop* VOCABULARY survives
--     as builder FNS (constructors are calls), the closed sum does not.
--   • The eq / forall PRESENTATIONS (`PropEq` / `PropForall`) survive as
--     `$tag` MARKER shapes authored at the TS `$`-key boundary (`prover.ts`
--     `propEq` / `propForall` — a `.fenel` body cannot author `$tag` and the
--     kernel's presentation rules read `$tag`); the kernel's Refl / Sample
--     rules key on those tags STRUCTURALLY (no registry lookup).
--   • The PROOF side (`Refl` / `DecidableSetResult` / `SampleTestResult`)
--     likewise survives as `$tag` marker shapes (TS `reflProof` /
--     `decidableSetProof` / `sampleTestProof`); the kernel's evidence
--     classifier (`evidenceOfProofTerm`) reads the tag string. The
--     Evidence-as-registered-ADT is deferred until a Fenel producer needs to
--     AUTHOR proof terms (none does — the proposers emit plain markers the TS
--     seam maps).
--
-- Pattern matching over these tags (structuralPropose's arms, the kernel
-- ladders) is STRUCTURAL — tag-only patterns match `$tag` with no registry
-- entity needed, so retiring the decls changes no dispatch.

-- UnprovedReason — the structured Err payload a proposer returns when it
-- declines (out-of-scope / undecided / budget / a refuting witness).
UnprovedReason = OutOfScope note: String
  | Undecided note: String
  | BudgetExceeded note: String
  | WitnessError counterexample: Anything

-- EpistemicStatus — the Ok payload the kernel attaches (grades the evidence).
EpistemicStatus = Proven
  | SolverChecked
  | SampleTested samplesChecked: Number
  | Assumed
  | Conjectured
  | Unknown
  | Refuted counterexample: Anything

-- VerifyError — the kernel's structured rejection payload.
VerifyError = ShapeMismatch reason: String propositionTag: String proofTag: String
  | WitnessRejected reason: String
  | UnknownRule reason: String

-- PropMonotonic — registered as a SEPARATE 1-case entity to make the "open
-- extension" pattern explicit: the closed Proposition sum stays unchanged; new
-- shapes are first-class ADTs declared alongside, with a Prover instance
-- dispatching on their `$tag`. `@discriminator "$tag"` forces the single-ctor
-- decl to stay a `$variant` (rather than collapse to a `$record`) so its
-- case-name roster reads ["PropMonotonic"] — the retired inline-literal shape
-- proposition-fenel-type.test.ts asserts; `$tag` is the default discriminator
-- (case-to-tag migration), a semantic no-op for downstream consumers.
@discriminator "$tag"
PropMonotonic = PropMonotonic agg: String

-- ProofStrategy — the two proof strategies (expr-substrate Phase 6b). The 8
-- per-proposition-shape Prover instances (Prover PropSubset, Prover PropEq, …)
-- COLLAPSE to two: `Prover Structural` (ONE prover dispatched internally by
-- proposition shape — `structuralPropose` in routers.fenel, routing each
-- Prop* shape to its proposer) + `Prover Smt` (the external-solver bridge
-- slot — `smtPropose`, an honest OutOfScope stub until the post-workstream
-- SMT arc). LLM / human / external proof sources are NOT strategies — they
-- call `kernel:verify` directly (the kernel is the single trust gate).
ProofStrategy = Structural | Smt

-- ----- Foreign declarations (native-backed; impl in ffi/prover-ffi.ts) -----

-- The 4 *Propose proposers: id `prover:<name>`, codeName + native-map key
-- `<name>Propose` (the codeName≠fnId-suffix reconciliation — @codeName).

@native
@codeName "decidableSetProverPropose"
@label "DecidableSetProver — PropSubset / PropDisjoint / PropEmpty"
@description "Untrusted proposer for PropSubset / PropDisjoint / PropEmpty propositions. Calls the Phase 3 DecidableMembership decision procedures and wraps the tri-state MaybeBool outcome as a kernel-verifiable DecidableSetResult proof term (on `Just true`) or a structured Err (on `Just false` or `Nothing`)."
@tags "prover" "decidable" "set-algebra"
decidableSetProver : (proposition: Any) -> Result UnprovedReason Any

@native
@codeName "reductionProverPropose"
@label "ReductionProver — PropEq via evaluator reduction"
@description "Untrusted proposer for PropEq propositions decided by reducing both sides through the evaluator and comparing with deepEqual. Emits a Refl proof term keyed off the reduced value; the kernel re-checks the equality."
@tags "prover" "reduction" "eq"
reductionProver : (proposition: Any) -> Result UnprovedReason Any

@native
@codeName "sampleTestProverPropose"
@label "SampleTestProver — PropForall via Phase 9.2 sample iteration"
@description "Generic untrusted proposer for PropForall propositions. Preserves proposition/sample presence and budget checks, then returns Undecided: this entry does not evaluate the named property, so inline samples alone cannot become SampleTested evidence. Genuine sample-law discharge uses its existing property-evaluation path."
@tags "prover" "sample-test" "forall"
sampleTestProver : (proposition: Any) -> Result UnprovedReason Any

@native
@codeName "monotonicityProverPropose"
@label "MonotonicityProver — PropMonotonic via Aggregable lookup"
@description "Phase 12 worked example. Untrusted proposer for PropMonotonic propositions over a named Aggregable aggregator. Reads the aggregator's Aggregable.monotonicity field; on `Monotone` emits a SampleTestResult mapping onto the kernel's existing rule. Demonstrates that adding a new proposition shape is a pure-Fenel concern — no kernel rule extension, no TS-side glue per law."
@tags "prover" "monotonicity" "aggregable" "phase12-demo"
monotonicityProver : (proposition: Any) -> Result UnprovedReason Any

-- The 2 per-case checks: codeName == fnId-suffix (self-consistent — registry-
-- dispatched by compilable.ts / evaluator-class.ts via `prover:<name>`).

@native
@label "CompilableSemanticProver — per-case equivalence check"
@description "Phase 8 per-case proposer for the `compilable-semantic-equivalence` law. For one `(source, inputs)` case + the instance's `compile` function (the law passes the method value; the JS bridge compiles through `compileFenelToJs` whatever function it is given): compiles the source to JS, executes via `new Function`, evaluates the body directly, and deepEqual-compares. Returns `Just true` on agreement, `Just false` on a structural divergence or a hard error during compile/exec. The law-validator's existing Forall iteration aggregates per-case outcomes into a SampleTestResult the kernel re-checks; passing instances earn `SampleTested` epistemic status."
@tags "prover" "compilable" "sample-test" "semantic-equivalence"
compilableSemanticCheck : (testCase: Any, compileFnId: (CompileSource -> Result CompileError target)) -> Maybe Boolean

@native
@label "PartialEvaluatorSoundnessProver — per-case soundness check"
@description "Phase 8 per-case proposer for the `partial-evaluator-soundness` law: `evaluate(partialEval(e, ctx1), ctx2) ≡ evaluate(e, ctx1 ∪ ctx2)`. For one `(expr, ctx1, ctx2)` case: partial-evals the expression under `ctx1`, then evaluates the residual under `ctx2`; separately evaluates the expression under the merged context; deepEqual-compares. Returns `Just true` on agreement; `Just false` otherwise. The law-validator iterates samples; the kernel re-checks the SampleTestResult."
@tags "prover" "partial-evaluator" "sample-test" "soundness"
partialEvaluatorSoundnessCheck : (testCase: Any) -> Maybe Boolean

-- kernel:verify — the trust boundary. Authored as `prover:kernelVerify` under
-- the header, re-id'd to `kernel:verify` in the seam (cross-prefix). codeName
-- defaults to `kernelVerify`; no @category (derives "kernel" from the re-id'd id).

@native
@label "Kernel verify"
@description "Re-check a proof term against a proposition. Returns `Ok EpistemicStatus` on acceptance (the status grades the kind of evidence — Proven for Refl, SolverChecked for DecidableSetResult, SampleTested for SampleTestResult) or `Err VerifyError` with a structured rejection. The closed set of kernel rules is the trust boundary; new rules grow the TCB intentionally."
@tags "kernel" "verify" "proof" "trust-boundary"
kernelVerify : (proposition: Any, proof: Any) -> Result VerifyError EpistemicStatus
